    <h2>When to Call Your Clinician</h2>

    <p>Contact your healthcare provider if:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>You have bleeding, pain, or other concerns</li>
      <li>You have not felt movement by 24 weeks</li>
      <li>You are past your due date</li>
      <li>You have signs of labor before 37 weeks</li>
      <li>Your baby is moving less than usual, or has stopped moving</li>
      <li>You cannot keep fluids down because of vomiting</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Do not wait until the next day if your baby's movements change. The NHS advises calling your midwife or maternity unit immediately, even in the middle of the night.</p>

    <p><em>Sources: NHS, https://www.nhs.uk/pregnancy/keeping-well/your-babys-movements/</em></p>

